# ripgrep (agents' rg, Claude Code's Grep/Glob) and VS Code/Cursor's search panel read this file before .gitignore.
# assets/ is ignored by Git; its small text (receipts, proof descriptions, generation records, prompts: about 6 MB)
# should be searchable, its media (about 9 GB) not. So: bring the folder back, hide all in it, bring back only text.
!/assets/
/assets/**
!/assets/**/
!/assets/**/*.json
!/assets/**/*.txt
!/assets/**/*.md

# Machine data under assets/ that no search should wade through (7 of its 11.5 MB of text, 2026-11-18): the card
# tracks per frame, the speech lane's receipts per line, the sequence dumps and the timeline. The files are still
# there and are read by path by the tools that own them; a search simply does not list them.
/assets/tracking/
/assets/speech/
/assets/sequences/
/assets/timeline.json

# Receipts of studies that are over (the p4 method studies, the archive move, the first public release). Nothing reads
# them by name; tools/media-audit.ts reads the folder by path. Hidden from search until Jakob has said whether the
# folder is to be taken out of Git (its history keeps it).
/evidence/

# Models and other binaries, wherever they land (Jakob 2026-11-18: "glb-modeller och andra stora filer ignoreras för
# att spara pengar"). .gitignore already hides most of them; these lines hold even if that file changes. Lock files and
# the 3D dummy's motion data (dealer3d/data/, 3 MB of numbers per frame) are text no search should read. All of it
# is still read by path by the tools that own it.
*.glb
*.gltf
*.bin
*.fbx
*.obj
*.blend
*.usdz
*.ply
*.stl
*.ktx2
*.hdr
*.exr
*.onnx
*.task
*.safetensors
*.wasm
package-lock.json
/dealer3d/data/
/dealer3d/standard/

# The paused dealer's film registers (Pamela, paused by Jakob 2026-11-12): 147 files that a search for a film or a
# seat should not mix with Paow's. Take the line out the day she is taken up again.
/motions/pamela-*

# Library code, not the project's own: three.js as brought in with the card material study, and the two built pages of
# that study (three.js plus about 300 lines of ours each). 163 000 lines that no search should wade through.
/materials/kortmaterial.js
/materials/markermaterial.js
/materials/source/references/card-materials/vendor/three.module.js
